19:T692,## State and behaviour, together

**Encapsulation** is the first pillar of OOP: bundle an object's **data** with the **methods that operate on it** into one unit, then **hide the internals** so the outside world can only touch them through a controlled door.

A class isn't just a bag of fields, it's fields *plus* the code that keeps those fields sane.

## Information hiding

Mark the data **private** (`-`) so nothing outside the class can read or write it directly:

```
class BankAccount {
    private int balance;          // nobody touches this directly
    public void withdraw(int amt) {
        if (amt > balance) throw new Error("insufficient");
        balance -= amt;           // the ONLY place balance changes
    }
}
```

The fields are **locked away**. The `public` methods are the **only door** in or out.

## Protecting invariants

The payoff is the **invariant**, a rule that must *always* hold, like **balance is never negative**. Because every change flows through `withdraw()` / `deposit()`, and those methods **validate** first, the object can never end up in an invalid state.

- Use **getters** to expose a read-only view, **setters** with validation to gate writes.
- Reject bad input at the boundary, the object **guards its own rules**.

## Why it pays off

- **Change internals freely.** Swap `int balance` for a `BigDecimal`, add caching, callers never notice, because they only ever saw the public interface.
- **Prevent invalid state by construction.** If the only way in validates, broken state is *unreachable*.

> Rule of thumb: make fields **private** until something forces you otherwise. A small, well-guarded public surface is the whole game.c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-foundations","activeLesson":"encapsulation"}],["$","$L18","encapsulation",{"lesson":{"id":"encapsulation","patternId":"lld-foundations","title":"Encapsulation","kind":"concept","difficulty":"Intro","statement":"Bundle data with the methods that guard it, hide the internals, and expose only a safe public interface, so invariants can’t be broken.","companies":["Amazon","Microsoft","Bloomberg"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"The capsule","code":["class BankAccount {","    private int balance;","    private String pin;","","    public void deposit(int amt) { ... }","    public void withdraw(int amt) {","        if (amt > balance) throw new Error();","        balance -= amt;","    }","    public int getBalance() { return balance; }","}"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":2,"narration":"Here is one capsule: BankAccount. The middle rows are its data, balance and pin, each marked with a “−”. That dash means PRIVATE: locked away, unreachable from outside.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"acct","name":"BankAccount","fields":["- balance: int","- pin: String"],"methods":["+ deposit(amt)","+ withdraw(amt)","+ getBalance()"],"x":1,"y":0.4,"tint":"accent"}],"relations":[],"shownClassIds":["acct"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["acct"]},"vars":[["−","private (hidden)"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":6,"narration":"The bottom rows are the public methods, marked “+”. deposit, withdraw, getBalance, this is the ONLY legal way in or out. Every interaction has to go through one of these doors.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["acct"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["acct"]},"vars":[["+","public (the door)"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":7,"narration":"And here is the point: withdraw() checks funds before subtracting, so balance can NEVER go negative. The object guards its own rules, the invariant holds because nothing else can touch balance.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["acct"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["acct"]},"vars":[["invariant","balance ≥ 0 always"]]},{"view":"class","narration":"Data plus the code that protects it, sealed in one capsule. Hide the internals, expose a small safe interface, that is encapsulation in a single box.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["acct"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":[]},"vars":[["capsule","data + its guards"]]}]},{"label":"Why hide it","code":["acct.balance = -999;   // ✗ compile error: balance is private","","acct.withdraw(50);     // ✓ the only legal path","    // inside: check funds, then subtract","return \"ok, 50\";"],"steps":[{"view":"sequence","codeLine":1,"narration":"Two lifelines: a Client and a BankAccount. Watch what happens when the Client tries to bypass the door versus going through it.","sequence":{"actors":[{"id":"client","label":"Client","kind":"actor"},{"id":"acct","label":"BankAccount"}],"messages":[{"id":"m1","from":"client","to":"acct","label":"balance = -999  ✗","kind":"call"},{"id":"m2","from":"client","to":"acct","label":"withdraw(50)","kind":"call"},{"id":"m3","from":"acct","to":"acct","label":"check funds","kind":"self"},{"id":"m4","from":"acct","to":"client","label":"ok, 50","kind":"return"}],"shownCount":0,"activeIndex":-1},"vars":[["lifeline","one object over time"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":1,"narration":"The Client reaches in to set the private field directly: balance = -999. This is a COMPILE ERROR, encapsulation forbids it. The field is private; there is no door here.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":1,"activeIndex":0},"vars":[["acct.balance =","✗ private"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":3,"narration":"The legal path instead goes through withdraw(50). Inside, the object makes a self-call to validate, “check funds”, before it dares change anything.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":3,"activeIndex":1},"vars":[["↺ self","validate first"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":5,"narration":"Funds are fine, so withdraw succeeds and returns “ok, 50”. Controlled access, every write validated, no back doors, keeps the object always-valid. That is why we hide it.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:sequence:messages","shownCount":4,"activeIndex":3},"vars":[["result","always-valid object"]]}]}]}}]]}]
